greps `aggregate_findings` over `tests` excluding only release-notes/adr/experiments/fixtures — this file is in scope","AC9 `make verify` would fail on the orphaned import"],"finding":"The plan's premise that `aggregate_findings` 'has no src caller (ADR 0108 :123)' is true, but it is used to justify `git rm aggregate.py` (step 6) without accounting for TEST callers. `tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py` has two live tests that import and exercise `aggregate_findings` (`test_aggregate_findings_clusters_and_ranks` at :438 and `test_aggregate_clusters_across_line_bucket_boundary` at :473, both `from rebar.llm.aggregate import aggregate_findings`). Deleting `aggregate.py` orphans both: `make verify` (AC9) breaks at import, and AC1's `aggregate_findings` grep over `tests/` returns matches.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fdd9b3107d2bcec67","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Approach step 6 / Testing section; tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py:438-515","norm_id":"n6773bb7676c9fec2","priority":0.9,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Running AC1's grep after the rm — it prints the two test hits","make verify collects test_llm_framework.py and errors at import of the deleted module"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"In step 6, add: delete `test_aggregate_findings_clusters_and_ranks` and `test_aggregate_clusters_across_line_bucket_boundary` from tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py (or move the two clustering tests to cover spec_scan's relocated `_severity_rank` if that behavior must stay covered).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.9,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"omits_required_site","dod_uncertifiable":"certification_cannot_prove","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"high","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.75,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Reproduce the per-file `ticket-quality`/`ticket_quality`/`_review_ticket_impl` edit list inline in the plan (not only in a comment), covering at minimum test_llm_framework.py (:49 default assertion, :75-80 select_reviewers golden table, :705 live call), test_review_ops_characterization.py:27/44/73, test_gate_source_threading.py, test_attested_signing.py, test_snapshot_environments.py, test_agent_op_safeguard.py, the test_prompt_* / test_execution_mode / test_new_eval_specs / test_eval_solver suites, test_generated_surface_markers.py, and test_review_skeleton.py:104/117.","cohort":["E4"],"criteria":["E4"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.05,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan Testing: 'The exact per-file delete/rewrite/swap list is in this ticket's first comment'","Plan body names only test_review_budget.py, test_review_as_workflow.py, test_subcall_class_selection.py, test_pydantic_ai_cutover_live.py","Live hits: test_llm_framework.py:49 `catalog['ticket-quality'].default is True`, :75-80 select_reviewers golden table, :705 `_review_ticket_impl`; test_review_ops_characterization.py:27/44/73 `_review_ticket_impl`; test_review_skeleton.py:104 `{'ticket-quality','tests','security'} <= batched`","AC1 scope `src tests docs scripts` excludes only docs/release-notes.md, docs/adr, docs/experiments, tests/fixtures — all the above are in scope"],"finding":"The plan's Testing section defers the 'exact per-file delete/rewrite/swap list' to 'this ticket's first comment,' but the plan text itself enumerates only four test files, while AC1's grep scope (`src tests docs scripts`, excluding only release-notes/adr/experiments/fixtures) contains many unnamed in-scope files with live `ticket-quality` / `_review_ticket_impl` hits that AC1 would flag. Concrete unaddressed-in-plan sites include tests/interfaces/store/test_llm_framework.py (`catalog['ticket-quality'].default is True` :49, the `select_reviewers` golden table :75-80, `_review_ticket_impl` :705), tests/interfaces/contracts/test_review_ops_characterization.py:27/44/73, tests/interfaces/store/test_gate_source_threading.py:103/127/151, test_attested_signing.py:217, test_snapshot_environments.py:137, test_agent_op_safeguard.py:86, test_eval_solver.py, test_new_eval_specs.py, the test_prompt_* suite, test_execution_mode.py, test_generated_surface_markers.py:130, and tests/unit/workflow/test_review_skeleton.py:104/117. The referenced comment is not reproduced in the plan and no resolvable ticket id is given (e2ed08b is a commit SHA), so the completeness of AC1/AC9 compliance cannot be verified from the plan text.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f453d9214434a9cca","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Testing section ('the exact per-file ... list is in this ticket's first comment'); Acceptance Criteria AC1 + AC9","norm_id":"n72e10c66d0754c23","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Running AC1's grep on the branch — it returns dozens of `ticket-quality` / `_review_ticket_impl` hits in files the plan never names","make verify collects the golden-table and default-assertion tests, which still assert the old `ticket-quality` catalog/default"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_ca